WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.360
[intro music]

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.820
[paddling sounds]

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.120
Good morning, John. It's Monday, February 12,
and I'm back in Montana. Can't you tell?

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.780
Actually, I'm probably on a plane right
now on my way to Montana.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:29.420
Either that or I'm in Montana trying to chip through about 3 inches of ice that formed on my sidewalk.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.240
This is pretty much the most beautiful day
that I'm going to see for a long time,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.420
so I figured I'd make my video a little early so
you could see me in Florida,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:45.200
doing Florida things, in a Florida hat, in
a Florida kayak, on a Florida intercoastal waterway,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.560
surrounded by Florida birds, Florida fish, and
Floridians, aaanddd...

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.960
mmeee...

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.280
and Katherine

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.400
[paddling noises]

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.160
Well, it's official. You're going to be getting this
video blog while I'm on a plane.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.920
I think it's the short leg, the one
from Denver to Missoula.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.260
And I'm in Denver right now.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.220
I am, as you know, a little bit of an amateur naturalist, and I'm a huge fan of birds

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.180
and also a huge fan of taking pictures of birds.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.740
So I wanted to share with you some of the birds that I saw and took pictures of while on my "vacation.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.620
tour of Florida."

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.960
Osprey, Black Crown Night Herons, Yellow Crown Night Herons, Little Blue Herons, Great Blue Herons,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.020
Tricolored Herons, Snowy Egrets, Great Egrets, Cormorants, Anhingas, Ibis, Muscovy Ducks,

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.220
and, most awesomely, this Limpkin, who pretty much just danced around me

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.900
letting me take awesome pictures of it, even though they're one of the most rare species of bird in Florida,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.800
and almost went extinct in the early 1900's.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.320
I made another interesting discovery
while here in Florida.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.800
While visiting my old college, I stopped by my old 7-11, and I found a beverage that you might be interested in.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.800
Katherine and I are still on the yearly "tour of the entire Southeastern United States"

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.640
and I've been looking at liquor stores wherever I go trying to find

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.360
Boone's Farm Strawberry Hill Flavored Citrus Wine.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.560
I'm at the 7-11 next to my old college and I have found Strawberry Hill. I'm about to buy it

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.040
so that I can complete the Strawberry Hill challenge, finally.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.820
It looks really gross and it costs...
it doesn't say how much it costs,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.820
but I only have 5 minutes left to buy it.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.380
5 minutes to spare!

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.140
That's kind of exciting!

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.200
Man: Are you guys saying there's only
5 minutes left to buy beer?

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:26.940
Hank: Yeah.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.820
Hank: Hurry!
Man: I better hurry and make my decision, huh?

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:35.760
Because you can't sell alcohol on Sundays in the state of Florida, so I have to buy this right now or else I'm not gonna get it.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:36.640
Bye.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.860
But you're gonna have to wait until Wednesday to see the completion of the Strawberry Hill challenge,

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.060
because I don't have time to edit it here in this airport.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.620
So, you'll see me on Wednesday, drinking Strawberry Hill, and I'll see you tomorrow.

